      "math_academy_id": "q-302650",
      "knowledge_point_id": "7f458c61-bc51-5653-9ecb-1e96eb5c335e",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Limit of an Inverse Trigonometric Function at a Point",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{\\pi x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/fc06a4e63f38a315dd3944f65f871cca2dbdddee26ec268e857f79e5f4ab8848.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{\\pi x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)}{\\pi \\cdot (1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{4}"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "\\frac{1}{4}",
          "choices_complete": false,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-302650",
        "kp_title": "Finding the Limit of an Inverse Trigonometric Function at a Point",
        "kp_href": null
